Sprint: Sanity v3 Curriculum Research (Root Category Model)
Scope Contract 1: catalogueRoot Research
Definition: Research and document the foundational catalogueRoot document type, establishing the mathematical reality of a top-level entity in Sanity v3.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Concept: Define catalogueRoot as a standalone document type in Sanity Studio, acting as the primary entry point for a specific catalog tree (e.g., "Headphones").

[ ] Document Syntax: Extract the exact TypeScript schema definition for a standard document type in Sanity v3.

[ ] Document Syntax Link: Locate and record the exact URL to the official Sanity v3 documentation for "document" types.

[ ] Document CRUD in CMS: Map the exact sequence of creating, reading, updating, and deleting a root document directly within the Sanity Studio UI.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the documented concept explicitly contrasts a root document against an object or array type.

[ ] Validate the syntax matches Next 15 / React 18 integration patterns (e.g., defineType).

Scope Contract 2: nesting array Research
Definition: Research and document the native Sanity array of objects, which serves as the primary mechanism for storing nested lists within a document.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Concept: Define the role of an array field containing custom objects within a Sanity document, including how Sanity stores this internally.

[ ] Document Syntax: Extract the exact TypeScript schema definition for an array field containing an object type.

[ ] Document Syntax Link: Locate and record the exact URL to the official Sanity v3 documentation for "array" types.

[ ] Document CRUD in CMS: Map the exact UI interactions for adding, reordering, editing, and removing items within an array field in Sanity Studio.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the syntax explicitly includes the of: [{ type: 'object' }] configuration.

Scope Contract 3: Relationship between catalogueRoot and nesting array
Definition: Research and document the architectural relationship and data flow when a nesting array is embedded directly inside a catalogueRoot document.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Concept: Define the parent-child relationship, explaining how the array belongs exclusively to the single root document (no external references needed).

[ ] Document Syntax: Extract the combined TypeScript schema showing the array defined as a field within the catalogueRoot document schema.

[ ] Document Syntax Link: Locate and record the exact URL to the official Sanity v3 documentation demonstrating nested fields within documents.

[ ] Document CRUD in CMS: Map how modifying the array items counts as an update to the parent catalogueRoot document (publishing the whole document vs. individual items).

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the conceptual breakdown explicitly addresses data fetching implications (e.g., fetching the root automatically fetches the nested array in GROQ).

Scope Contract 4: nesting level inside nesting array
Definition: Research and document the implementation of a second layer of nesting (an array of objects inside an object that is already inside an array).

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Concept: Define the recursive data structure concept within Sanity and the limitations or warnings regarding deep nesting in NoSQL document databases.

[ ] Document Syntax: Extract the TypeScript schema for an object that contains its own array field, which is then used as the type for the parent array.

[ ] Document Syntax Link: Locate and record the exact URL to the official Sanity v3 documentation regarding deep nesting and object types.

[ ] Document CRUD in CMS: Map the editor experience of opening an array item, and then opening a nested array item inside that modal/popover in Sanity Studio.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the CRUD documentation notes the UI UX limitations of nested modals in Sanity Studio.

Scope Contract 5: n+1 nesting array inside nested array
Definition: Research and document infinite or deep recursive nesting structures (e.g., categories within categories indefinitely) within a single Sanity document.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Concept: Define recursive schemas in Sanity v3 (a type referencing itself) and the maximum depth limits imposed by the platform.

[ ] Document Syntax: Extract the TypeScript schema utilizing defineType and self-referencing to achieve n+1 nesting.

[ ] Document Syntax Link: Locate and record the exact URL to the official Sanity v3 documentation for "recursive object types" or "trees".

[ ] Document CRUD in CMS: Map the performance and usability degradation of deep recursive editing in the CMS, identifying the practical depth limit for a human editor.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the documentation clearly outlines the exact depth at which Sanity Studio UI breaks or becomes unmanageable for web developers and editors.

Scope Contract 6: Curriculum Assembly and Synthesis
Definition: Consolidate the researched items into a professionally designed, sequential learning curriculum file for immediate practical application.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Create curriculum-sanity-vfs.md.

[ ] Format the output sequentially from Contract 1 to Contract 5.

[ ] Ensure no comments exist within any provided code blocks.

[ ] Strip out all theoretical fluff; retain only strict pragmatic math, direct syntax, and explicit Studio operational guides.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Read through the generated curriculum to guarantee it follows the sequence of achieving the next goal (root -> array -> relationship -> deep nesting).